cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  HUSH - Human genome Universal Silencing Hairpin-designer
message: If you use HUSH in your work, please cite it.
type: software
abstract: >-
  An allele-aware siRNA/shRNA design pipeline for polymorphic gene families.
  HUSH enumerates siRNA candidates from a target transcript, screens them
  against the classical efficacy rules and transcriptome off-target search,
  reasons over a panel of related sequences for broad or allele-specific
  knockdown, and converts survivors into cloneable stem-loop shRNA constructs.
  Developed as part of Project HIDE (HLA Interference through Disguise and
  Erasure).
